<config xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="urn:magento:module:Magento_Config:etc/system_file.xsd">
    <system>
        <section id="srcloudflare_images" translate="label" type="text" sortOrder="360"
                 showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
            <label>Cloudflare Images</label>
            <tab>studioraz</tab>
            <resource>SR_Cloudflare::srcloudflare_settings</resource>

            <group id="general" translate="label" type="text" sortOrder="1" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                <label>General</label>

                <field id="active" translate="label comment" sortOrder="100" type="select"
                       showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Enabled</label>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                    <comment>Enables Cloudflare image resizing for storefront images.</comment>
                    <config_path>srcloudflare/general/active</config_path>
                </field>

                <field id="image_quality" type="text" translate="label comment" sortOrder="200" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Image Quality</label>
                    <config_path>srcloudflare/general/image_quality</config_path>
                    <comment><![CDATA[Specifies quality for images in JPEG, WebP, and AVIF formats. The quality is in a 1-100 scale, but useful values are between <i>50</i> (low quality, small file size) and <i>90</i> (high quality, large file size). <i>85</i> is the default. When using the PNG format, an explicit quality setting allows use of PNG8 (palette) variant of the format.<br>See <a href="https://developers.cloudflare.com/images/image-resizing/url-format/#quality" target="_blank">Cloudflare documentation</a> for more information.]]></comment>
                </field>

                <field id="image_fit" type="select" translate="label comment" sortOrder="220" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Image Fit</label>
                    <source_model>SR\Cloudflare\Model\System\Config\Source\ImageFit</source_model>
                    <config_path>srcloudflare/general/image_fit</config_path>
                    <comment><![CDATA[Affects interpretation of <i>width</i> and <i>height</i>. All resizing modes preserve aspect ratio.<br>See <a href="https://developers.cloudflare.com/images/image-resizing/url-format/#fit" target="_blank">Cloudflare documentation</a> for more information.]]></comment>
                </field>
            </group>
        </section>

        <section id="srcloudflare" translate="label" type="text" sortOrder="350"
                 showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="0">
            <label>Cloudflare Cache</label>
            <tab>studioraz</tab>
            <resource>SR_Cloudflare::srcloudflare_settings</resource>

            <group id="cache" translate="label" type="text" sortOrder="10"
                   showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="0">
                <label>Cache (FPC)</label>

                <field id="active" translate="label" sortOrder="10" type="select"
                       showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="0" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Enabled</label>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                </field>

                <field id="account_id" translate="label comment" sortOrder="25" type="text"
                       showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0">
                    <label>Account ID</label>
                    <comment>Account ID from the Cloudflare dashboard. Magento uses it to discover zones and deploy the shared FPC Worker.</comment>
                    <validate>validate-alphanum</validate>
                </field>

                <field id="api_token" translate="label comment" sortOrder="30" type="obscure"
                       showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0">
                    <label>API Token</label>
                    <backend_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Backend\Encrypted</backend_model>
                    <comment><![CDATA[Use a Cloudflare Account API Token or User API Token with the following permissions for the configured account and its zones.<br>
                        <strong>Account → Workers Scripts → Edit</strong><br>
                        <strong>Zone → Zone → Read</strong><br>
                        <strong>Zone → Workers Routes → Edit</strong><br>
                        <strong>Zone → Cache Purge</strong><br>
                        The same token is used for deployments, routes, and cache invalidation.]]></comment>
                </field>

                <field id="worker_name" translate="label comment" sortOrder="32" type="text"
                       showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Worker Name</label>
                    <comment>Cloudflare name for the shared Worker. Set it before the first deployment.</comment>
                    <config_path>srcloudflare/worker/name</config_path>
                </field>

                <field id="worker_management" translate="label comment" sortOrder="34" type="text"
                       showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0">
                    <label>Worker Management</label>
                    <comment>Select zones for route configuration and cache purges, then save the configuration. All accessible zones are selected by default. Magento keeps purging deselected zones until Start Deploy clears their managed routes.</comment>
                    <frontend_model>SR\Cloudflare\Block\Adminhtml\System\Config\Worker</frontend_model>
                    <backend_model>SR\Cloudflare\Model\System\Config\Backend\ZoneSelection</backend_model>
                    <config_path>srcloudflare/cache/zone_selection</config_path>
                </field>

                <field id="debug" translate="label comment" sortOrder="100" type="select"
                       showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="0" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Debug</label>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                    <comment><![CDATA[Enables module diagnostics in <code>var/log/srcloudflarecache.log</code>. Credentials are excluded.]]></comment>
                    <depends>
                        <field id="active">1</field>
                    </depends>
                </field>

                <group id="magento_cache" translate="label" type="text" sortOrder="105"
                       showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0">
                    <label>Magento Cache</label>
                    <attribute type="expanded">1</attribute>

                    <field id="caching_application" extends="system/full_page_cache/caching_application"
                           translate="label comment" sortOrder="1" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0"
                           canRestore="1">
                        <comment>Select the global full-page cache application used by Magento.</comment>
                        <config_path>system/full_page_cache/caching_application</config_path>
                    </field>
                    <field id="ttl" extends="system/full_page_cache/ttl"
                           sortOrder="5" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0" canRestore="1">
                        <config_path>system/full_page_cache/ttl</config_path>
                    </field>
                </group>

                <group id="purge" translate="label" type="text" sortOrder="110"
                       showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="0">
                    <label>Purge Configuration</label>
                    <depends>
                        <field id="srcloudflare/cache/active">1</field>
                    </depends>

                    <field id="async_purge" translate="label comment" sortOrder="110" type="select"
                           showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="0" canRestore="1">
                        <label>Async Purge Queue</label>
                        <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                        <comment><![CDATA[Queues Magento cache tag purges and sends them from cron using Cloudflare Pro-safe throttling.]]></comment>
                        <config_path>srcloudflare/cache/async_purge</config_path>
                    </field>
                    <field id="purge_batch_size" translate="label comment" sortOrder="120" type="text"
                           showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="0" canRestore="1">
                        <label>Purge Batch Size</label>
                        <validate>validate-digits validate-greater-than-zero</validate>
                        <comment><![CDATA[Maximum Cloudflare purge operations per request. Cloudflare allows 100 for tag, hostname, prefix, and purge-everything requests; larger values are capped to 100.]]></comment>
                        <config_path>srcloudflare/cache/purge_batch_size</config_path>
                        <depends>
                            <field id="srcloudflare/cache/active">1</field>
                            <field id="async_purge">1</field>
                        </depends>
                    </field>
                    <field id="purge_max_requests_per_cron" translate="label comment" sortOrder="130" type="text"
                           showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="0" canRestore="1">
                        <label>Max Purge Requests Per Cron Run</label>
                        <validate>validate-digits validate-greater-than-zero</validate>
                        <comment><![CDATA[Default 25 matches the Cloudflare Pro purge bucket size. Cron runs every minute.]]></comment>
                        <config_path>srcloudflare/cache/purge_max_requests_per_cron</config_path>
                        <depends>
                            <field id="srcloudflare/cache/active">1</field>
                            <field id="async_purge">1</field>
                        </depends>
                    </field>
                    <field id="purge_max_attempts" translate="label comment" sortOrder="140" type="text"
                           showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="0" canRestore="1">
                        <label>Max Purge Attempts</label>
                        <validate>validate-digits validate-greater-than-zero</validate>
                        <comment><![CDATA[Queue rows are marked failed after this many unsuccessful API attempts.]]></comment>
                        <config_path>srcloudflare/cache/purge_max_attempts</config_path>
                        <depends>
                            <field id="srcloudflare/cache/active">1</field>
                            <field id="async_purge">1</field>
                        </depends>
                    </field>
                </group>

                <group id="worker" translate="label" type="text" sortOrder="400"
                       showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0">
                    <label>Worker Configuration</label>

                    <field id="debug" translate="label comment" sortOrder="10" type="select"
                           showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0" canRestore="1">
                        <label>Worker Debug Mode</label>
                        <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                        <comment>Enables diagnostic response headers after deployment.</comment>
                        <config_path>srcloudflare/worker/debug</config_path>
                    </field>
                    <field id="hfp_ttl" translate="label comment" sortOrder="30" type="text"
                           showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0" canRestore="1">
                        <label>Hit-For-Pass TTL (seconds)</label>
                        <validate>validate-digits</validate>
                        <comment>Lifetime of markers for responses the Worker cannot cache. Defaults to 120 seconds.</comment>
                        <config_path>srcloudflare/worker/hfp_ttl</config_path>
                    </field>
                    <field id="bypass_paths" translate="label comment" sortOrder="40" type="textarea"
                           showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0" canRestore="1">
                        <label>Additional Bypass Paths</label>
                        <comment><![CDATA[Enter paths such as <code>/api</code> or <code>/rest</code>, one per line or separated by commas. The Worker uses these paths to skip caching for matching requests. Save the configuration and run Start Deploy to apply changes.]]></comment>
                        <config_path>srcloudflare/worker/bypass_paths</config_path>
                    </field>
                </group>
            </group>

            <group id="worker_routes" translate="label" type="text" sortOrder="20"
                   showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0">
                <label>Worker Routes</label>

                <field id="default_bypass_routes" translate="label comment" sortOrder="10" type="label"
                       showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0">
                    <label>Built-in Bypass Routes</label>
                    <comment>Magento applies these exclusions during deployment. The Admin bypass is generated from the Magento Admin URL and is added where its hostname belongs to a selected zone.</comment>
                    <frontend_model>SR\Cloudflare\Block\Adminhtml\System\Config\DefaultWorkerRoutes</frontend_model>
                </field>

                <field id="bypass_paths" translate="label comment" sortOrder="20" type="text"
                       showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Additional Bypass Routes</label>
                    <comment><![CDATA[Add one path per row, such as <code>/api</code> or <code>/feeds</code>. Magento creates a route such as <code>/feeds/*</code> without a Worker for the domain and subdomains of each selected zone. Save the configuration and run Start Deploy to apply changes.]]></comment>
                    <frontend_model>SR\Cloudflare\Block\Adminhtml\System\Config\AdditionalBypassRoutes</frontend_model>
                    <backend_model>SR\Cloudflare\Model\System\Config\Backend\BypassRoutes</backend_model>
                </field>
            </group>
        </section>
    </system>
</config>
